An antichain cannot have both a set and its superset. So the largest antichain here would be the two subsets of size 1: {1}, {2}, which is size 2. Alternatively, the two subsets of size 1 are larger than the subsets of size 0 or 2. Since the binomial coefficient for 2 choose 1 is 2, which is indeed the maximum antichain. If we tried to take {1,2} and one of the singletons, that would also be size 2, but you can't have all three. So yes, 2 is the maximum. Which matches 2 choose 1 = 2.

